# win32u: Initialize text metrics in get_text_metr_size() on failure.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12397 state=opened
# If the font is selected but measuring it fails (for example with no font engine, as in a WoW64 setup without 32-bit FreeType), `NtGdiGetTextMetricsW()` leaves the TEXTMETRICW untouched, and `get_text_metr_size()` hands it back uninitialized.

`normalize_nonclientmetrics()` then computes the menu and caption heights from stack garbage and saves them to `HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop\WindowMetrics` (e.g. `MenuHeight=6750318` in a fresh prefix), which breaks window sizes. The SM_CXMENUCHECK/SM_CYMENUCHECK paths return garbage for the same reason.

This sets the same fallback values that are already used when the font can't be created or selected, so every caller gets defined metrics.

This supersedes !7316 by Ruslan Garipov (@ruslangaripov), which only covers `normalize_nonclientmetrics()`. He suggested opening a separate MR in  !7316#note_155078. Thanks to him for tracking down the cause.
--- dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -5481,10 +5481,11 @@ static void get_text_metr_size( HDC hdc, LOGFONTW *lf, TEXTMETRICW *metric, UINT
     TEXTMETRICW tm;
     UINT ret;
     if (!metric) metric = &tm;
+    metric->tmHeight = -1;
+    metric->tmExternalLeading = 0;
     hfont = NtGdiHfontCreate( lf, sizeof(*lf), 0, 0, NULL );
     if (!hfont || !(hfontsav = NtGdiSelectFont( hdc, hfont )))
     {
-        metric->tmHeight = -1;
         if (psz) *psz = 10;
         if (hfont) NtGdiDeleteObjectApp( hfont );
         return;

